186045417 true] [17592186427500 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427496 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427500 1079 #uuid "b5e7343a-4633-545d-a3b9-3c2ada585e3e" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427500 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1069 "q-184533" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1071 "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times [-1,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1072 #uuid "46ba7fa0-d231-5401-8252-d4e156d84cf4" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427501 1074 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(-1,-1),$ $(-1,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(1,-1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/71/712970edb9966d6544cbe4a360aaa0de3436f356c4c7f23ff601c70ef168a521.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times [-1,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-i,i],b\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(-i,-1),$ $(-i,1),$ $(i,1),$ and $(i,-1).$\n\n![](images/68/68f8c51062bd9d3ecadd33b0a67ea0990f631375aba9f9cc705946c79abf47d0.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [-1,1]:$\n\n![](images/ff/ffaa9807fa5155dcc848d68bed93a16b267045fae3f5d4d0945e064ad5c11eef.png)" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427502 1058 #edb/ref 17592186427506 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [17592186427502 1062 #uuid "2f868252-f8e0-5a5f-92f0-b020aafff313" 13194139534603 17592186045417 true] [1759218642